; Unit suites for the library's internal modules reach them through
; [Thumper.Private] — the facade's unconstrained re-export of the internals
; for this suite. No test compiles its own copy of a library unit: the
; library is built once and linked, so an edit to any lib/ source rebuilds
; exactly the tests that depend on it, under the library's own flags.
;
; Each test lists only the libraries its own source references
; (implicit_transitive_deps is false): [thumper] for the internals, [unix]
; where the test itself calls [Unix.*], [windtrap] everywhere.

(test
 (name test_thumper)
 ; Its slow tests measure on the real clock, so they take the cram
 ; sessions' lock.
 (modules test_thumper)
 (locks ../cram/measurement)
 (libraries thumper windtrap))

